 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Camp Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a summer camp registration form?\", \"a\": \"A summer camp registration form is what a parent completes to enroll a child in camp. It records the camper's details and the sessions chosen, along with the adults allowed at pickup. Many camps take payment and signed waivers on the same form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a summer camp registration form online?\", \"a\": \"List your sessions with their dates and prices, then the questions you ask about each camper. Describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it builds the online form with a payment step, plus a database of every camper who registers.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free summer camp registration form template?\", \"a\": \"Form builders and template sites offer free versions that cover the basics. Any template still needs your own sessions and prices added. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing your camp's form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a camp registration form take payment at signup?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Connect Stripe, and a parent pays a deposit or the whole fee in the same visit as the sign-up. Late balances are far easier to chase when every payment sits next to the child it covers.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I add sibling discounts to camp registration forms?\", \"a\": \"Write the discount as a rule. Tell Emergent that a second child gets 10% off, and the form works out each family's total before checkout. Parents see the lower price on screen, and the office stops correcting totals by hand.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up a waitlist on a camp registration form?\", \"a\": \"Give each session a limit, and the form stops taking payments for that week once it fills. Parents who arrive later join the waitlist instead. When a family cancels, the office emails the next name on the list and offers the spot.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a camp registration form include?\", \"a\": \"Start with the camper's name and grade, then a phone number and email for each parent. Staff also need allergies and swim level. Backup contacts can sit on a separate emergency contact form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can camp registration forms collect a signed waiver?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give the waiver its own step with a signature box, and name each activity it covers, such as swimming or archery. Collecting it at sign-up means no camper arrives without one. A standalone <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/liability-waiver-form'>liability waiver form</a> suits visitors who never register.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a church camp registration form template?\", \"a\": \"A church camp asks the same core questions as any other camp, plus a few of its own, such as the home congregation and the youth leader. Describe those to Emergent with your early-bird date, and the form sets the price by the day a parent submits.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a camp registration form collect medical information?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give allergies their own question, apart from any medicine a child takes each day, and request the dose and timing for each medicine. Counselors can then act on what a parent wrote without calling home. For sign-ups that need none of this, such as an open house, a plain <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/registration-form'>registration form</a> is enough.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}